**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Food Delivery**

---

## 1.  Goal Tables  

| ID | Title | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Enquired / Target | Relation |
|----|-------|------|---------|-----------|-------------------|----------|
| **G1** | Deliver food to inpatient room | Bring a meal from the kitchen to the patient’s room (either onto the table or via the tray). | **FALLBACK(G1.1, G1.2)** | Perform | – | **OR** |
| **G1.1** | Deliver food to room table | Place the meal directly on the patient’s table. | **;** | Perform | – | **AND** |
| **G1.1.1** | Open room door | Open the patient’s room door (robot‑only or with a human). | **FALLBACK(AT1, AT2)** | Perform | – | **OR** |
| **G1.1.2** | Place food on table | Robot places the meal onto the table. | **-** | Perform | – | **AND** |
| **G1.2** | Fetch food from robot tray | Retrieve a meal from the robot’s tray (requires patient/companion/nurse/robot help). | **;** | Perform | – | **AND** |
| **G1.2.0** | Query patient retrieval capability | Determine if the patient can fetch the meal, and whether a companion or nurse is present. | **-** | **Query** | patient status, presence of companion or nurse | **AND** |
| **G1.2.1** | Request assistance | Ask the appropriate party to retrieve the meal. | **OR** | Perform | – | **OR** |
| **G1.2.2** | Record meal retrieval | Log the meal‑retrieval event (time, patient ID, meal ID). | **-** | Perform | – | **AND** |
| **G1.2.3** | Detect wrong meal retrieval | Verify that the patient has retrieved the correct meal. | **-** | Perform | – | **AND** |
| **G1.3** | Retrieve dirty dishes | Pick up and remove dirty dishes from the patient’s room. | **;** | Perform | – | **AND** |
| **G1.3.1** | Open room door (dish retrieval) | Open the patient’s room door for dish pickup (robot‑only or with a human). | **FALLBACK(AT13, AT14)** | Perform | – | **OR** |
| **G1.3.2** | Pick up dishes | Pick up dishes (alone, with a human, or with another robot). | **OR** | Perform | – | **OR** |

